#             Cleared 2 top-level StringPattern entries (repl_hosted, repl_navigation)
#             — both shifted to new blockers (see below).
#             5 nested-StringPattern entries shifted to Unit ctor field blocker.
#             1 new xfail added: test_ir_codegen_string_pattern.spr (same Unit ctor
#             field blocker as the other test_ir_codegen_* files).
#             list_pattern_demo shifted to nested BoolPattern (StringPattern cleared).
#   PR 15e — Unit ctor field as i64 0 sentinel  ✓ this PR
#             5 test_ir_codegen_* entries unblocked from Unit ctor field error.
#             All 5 + 1 new test (test_ir_codegen_unit_ctor_field) shifted to
#             pre-existing '%else_27' undefined-value bug (match-arm label/scope gap
#             in stdlib.compiler IR; same family as '%body_*' gap).
#
# Bucket breakdown after PR 15e closes (re-probed):
#    ~6 entries — IR codegen OOM on CI (>2 GB peak RSS).  The 6 test_ir_codegen_*
#                 tests below construct hand-built IRPrograms, which forces them
#                 to `import stdlib.compiler` — pulling the entire self-hosted
#                 compiler into the compile unit.  --use-ir-codegen keeps the
#                 full IRBlock/IROp graph in memory before lowering (vs. direct
#                 codegen's streaming Emitter at ~160 MB/file), so per-file peak
#                 RSS is 2-2.6 GB and CI runners OOM.  This is an *architectural*
#                 cost of the typed IR design, not a per-file defect — the tests
#                 pass under direct codegen and would clear their logical XFAIL
#                 reason if probed on a beefier host.  Tracked as BACKLOG §1
#                 "stream IR codegen output per-function (don't materialize full
#                 IRProgram)" — P1 M5 prep work.  All new tests that import
#                 stdlib.compiler MUST be added here with this OOM reason until
#                 the streaming fix lands; they cannot be probed on CI.
#                 Logical-blocker underneath: PR 15e cleared the Unit ctor field
#                 error; the next probe would surface '%else_27' (match-arm
#                 label/scope gap in translate_do — fixed in PR 15f) — but on
#                 CI the OOM trips first regardless of logical state.
#    ~1 entry   — translate_do drops match blocks in non-last do steps
#                 (IR invalid: use of undefined value '%arm_0_N'; test_repl_navigation)
#    ~1 entry   — @analysis_check_source undefined (repl_hosted; unresolved extern)
#    ~1 entry   — nested BoolPattern in constructor match (list_pattern_demo)
#    ~2 entries — pre-existing 't0' dup-block (codegen idx bug; pre-existing)
#    ~3 entries — typeclass `__unresolved_Eq__` / `__unresolved_ToString__`
#                 (typeclass dispatch gap — same family as @append)
#    ~1 entry  — @append undefined (Semigroup dispatch; same family as above)
#    ~1 entry  — `range not yet supported` (ast_to_ir TRange case)
#    ~2 entries — nested IntPattern in ctor match (PR 8 follow-up)
#    ~2 entries — pre-existing direct-codegen xfails (unresolved name in source)
#    ~2 entries — use of undefined value '%body_*' (match-arm label/scope gap)

